#: manual/index.md:15
msgid "At a glance"
msgstr ""

#: manual/index.md:17
msgid "`Quaternion[T]` is generic in its component type. Ring operations work over exact types such as `Int`; functions that need square roots or trigonometry compute in `Double` through `DoubleConvert`, which is implemented for `Int` and `Double`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/index.md:18
msgid "`+`, `-`, unary `-` and `*` (the Hamilton product) are the usual operations. `*` is not commutative."
msgstr ""

#: manual/index.md:19
msgid "`q / r` is right division $q\\,r^{-1}$; `q.left_div(r)` is left division $r^{-1} q$. Before 0.2.0, `/` computed $r^{-1} q$."
msgstr ""

#: manual/index.md:20
msgid "The type implements luna-generic's `Zero`, `One`, `AddMonoid`, `MulMonoid`, `Semiring`, `Ring`, `Inverse` and `Conjugate`. It does not implement `Field`, because multiplication is not commutative."
msgstr ""

#: manual/index.md:21
msgid "Rotations: `from_axis_angle`, `from_euler`, `Quaternion::rotate`, `slerp`, `Quaternion::to_euler` and its eight fixed-order variants."
msgstr ""

